{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdC8oPGL3tr1toNkn2BF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the candidate `personal_overalternation_leniency`, and the self-check passed (`OK`). It refines the incumbent `asymmetric_tolerance_lopsided_stretch`.\n\n**What changed:** In the incumbent, everyone shares one fraction that sets how much less it costs to switch more often than your ideal rate than to switch less often. In my version each person has their own fraction, drawn from a population (log-normal, written in the non-centred form so it samples smoothly). Everything else is the incumbent's, unchanged. So some people barely mind a sequence that alternates more than they expect, while others reject it as firmly as a streaky one. That is separate from where each person's ideal switching rate lies.\n\n**Self-check results:**\n- **ELPD-LOO:** -3493.1 on the short smoke fit, against the incumbent's -3500.3. The smoke fit is only 100 draws on one chain, so this is not a real comparison yet.\n- **PSIS-LOO looks unreliable:** 8.7% of trials have Pareto k above 0.5, far over the 1% tolerance. On the full fit this could mean the model is flagged as unreliable, and then it can't be exported as the winner.\n- **Not checked:** convergence (a single chain can't report R-hat) and novelty against the live models. The novelty check averages predictions over participants, so a per-person effect could mostly cancel out there; I haven't tested whether it stays above the 0.002 threshold.\n\nAfter the check passed I deleted one leftover comment line from `candidate.py`. The edit touched only the comment, so I didn't re-run the check.\n\n**Why not the critique's side bias:** The critique's only finding is that people's own left-choice rates vary more than the incumbent produces, and it doesn't survive the FDR correction (q = 0.128). Adding a personal side bias gained only 0.6 nats on the previous best model. It's also the obvious fix, and the other incumbent-refinement slot seemed likely to try it.\n\nFiles are in `experiment3/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_3/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3411,"cache_read_input_tokens":82653,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3411,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b18e481f-06b4-4b2b-831a-86aaef1a1fa2","uuid":"655c07e0-39d4-4acd-a563-ef76f4532408","timestamp":"2026-10-02T09:42:57.426Z","request_id":"req_011CfdC8nyDkBaqs1W3AZNw1"}
